WEBVTT

00:00:00.759 --> 00:00:08.758
Start page: new, open, examples. Click "Open" and open the WQ-LS lockstitch machine

00:00:08.758 --> 00:00:13.657
At the top is the menu bar: File, Edit, View, Tools… every command is here

00:00:13.657 --> 00:00:19.757
Below it, the toolbars: buttons for common commands. Hover over a button to see what it does

00:00:19.757 --> 00:00:27.257
The workbench selector: Part Design, Sketcher, Assembly, TechDraw, FEM… switch workbench and the toolbars change

00:00:27.257 --> 00:00:33.257
Top left, the model tree: every object in the file. WQ-LS is grouped into eight assemblies

00:00:33.257 --> 00:00:39.182
Bottom left, the properties: select an object to see its placement, colour and dimensions

00:00:39.182 --> 00:00:44.182
The big area in the middle is the 3D view, where you look at and pick parts

00:00:44.182 --> 00:00:49.008
Top right, the navigation cube: click a face to look from that direction

00:00:49.008 --> 00:00:54.607
Report view: messages, warnings and errors appear here (View → Panels → Report view)

00:00:54.607 --> 00:01:00.332
At the bottom, the status bar: what the mouse is over, the navigation style, the units

00:01:00.332 --> 00:01:07.160
That is the FreeCAD interface. WenQuest CAD is built on it, so it looks the same
